          %h1#links Links
          %h2#references References
          %p The topological topos was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em Topos Theory
                , Academic Press New York 1977. (Dover reprint 2014; exercise 0.10, p.21)
            %li#Johnstone79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                %em On a topological topos
                , Proc. London Math. Soc. (3)
                %strong 38
                (1979) 237-271 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://plms.oxfordjournals.org/content/s3-38/2/237.full.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review (with somewhat terminology):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant+--+A+Topos+Theory+Compendium"} Sketches of an Elephant – A Topos Theory Compendium
              %blockquote
                %p see A2.1.11(j), A2.6.4(c), C2.2.14(b); pp. 81, 123,537f
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient categories of spaces
          %ul
            %li
              H. A. Harasani,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Johnstone’s topos
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topos theoretic methods in general topology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://groupoids.org.uk/harasani.html"} web
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://groupoids.org.uk/pdffiles/HarasaniPhD-V-VI-Bib.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also discussion at:
          %ul
            %li
              n-cafe
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2014/04/on_a_topological_topos.html"} blog on Johnstone’s paper
          %p
            Proof that the topological topos satisfies
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+choice"} dependent choice
          %ul
            %li#ShulmanSimpson2024
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"} Alex Simpson
              %em Dependent choice in Johnstone’s topological topos
              (2024) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "/nlab/files/DCTopTopos.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A
            = succeed "-analogue" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos"} higher topos
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Shulman"}> Michael Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Brouwer’s fixed-point theorem in real-cohesive homotopy type theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.07584"} arXiv:1509.07584
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mart%C3%ADn+Escard%C3%B3"}> Martín Escardó
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The intrinsic topology of Martin-Lof universes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cs.bham.ac.uk/~mhe/papers/universe-indiscrete.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bas+Spitters"}> Bas Spitters
                ,
                %em Cubical sets and the topological topos
                , arXiv:1610.05270 (2016). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.05270"}> abstract
                )
          %p Generalizations of its construction occur in the following two papers:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                R. Montañez,
                %em Topoi generated by topological spaces
                , Talk CT15 Aveiro (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://sweet.ua.pt/dirk/ct2015/slides/Montanez.pdf"}> pdf-slides
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                C. Ruiz, R. Montañez,
                %em Elevadores de Estructura
                , Boletín de Matemáticas
                %strong XIII
                2 (2006) 111-135. &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.revistas.unal.edu.co/index.php/bolma/article/view/40451"}> link
                \&amp;rbrack;
